The viable family is now sharper than the initial colouring idea: Theorem 3.1 characterizes the balanced odd-\(\Delta\) graphs with chromatic index \(\Delta\) by a matching covering every maximum-degree vertex. I’ll generate a balanced regular bipartite signed graph as the union of three projective-linear perfect matchings, and ask for one matching as a normalized \(2\times2\) matrix over \(\mathbb F_p\). This keeps the answer at four field elements while the graph and the standard recovery cost grow with \(p\).
