codex
The newer on-disk implementation is the stronger paper-native choice, so I’m retaining it: it asks for the actual \(S^0_\Delta\) signed edge-colouring rather than an auxiliary matching encoding. Its measured gates already pass, including 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses and five attacks at 0/8; the disclosed König decomposition solves 8/8 in about 5,621 operations, versus 237 operations for the reciprocal-coordinate route. I’m starting the required bare four-vendor hardening ladder now.
