All local gates pass:

- G1: 12/12 planted certificates verified
- G4: 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses
- G6: five attacks at 0/8; reference algorithm solves 8/8
- G8: 140/140 invariance checks
- G9: 571 characters, 228 atoms, 237 intended operations

The result is not yet submission-ready: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” before any scored oracle call in all three hardening arms. The harness-owned error transcripts were preserved, but they are not hardness evidence. Raising the OpenRouter key limit and rerunning STEP 4 and both G9 arms is the remaining blocker.
